= Logic — Simple =

'''Logic''' studies when conclusions follow from reasons or premises.

A logical system usually has rules for writing statements, rules for making deductions, and a way to say what the statements mean.

A valid argument is one where the conclusion follows from the premises.

That does not mean the premises are true.

There are many kinds of logic. Classical logic is important, but it is not the only logic.

Examples include propositional logic, first-order logic, and modal logic.

